###############################################################################
# Haku VR Museum — repo root ignore rules.
#
# One file covers the whole repo: the Unity project under unity/ and the Python
# service under ai-service/.
#
# 🚨 ANCHORING, READ THIS BEFORE EDITING. GitHub's canonical Unity.gitignore
# uses leading-slash patterns (/[Ll]ibrary/) that anchor to the directory
# holding the .gitignore. Pasted at a repo root those NEVER match
# unity/Library/, and someone pushes a multi-gigabyte Library folder. Every
# Unity pattern below is therefore written WITHOUT a leading slash, so it
# matches at any depth. Once unity/ exists, prove it:
#
#     git check-ignore -v unity/Library/ArtifactDB
#
# That must print a matching rule. Silence means this file is broken.
###############################################################################

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unity 6000.5.5f1 — generated caches, imports and build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
[Ll]ibrary/
[Tt]emp/
[Oo]bj/
[Bb]uild/
[Bb]uilds/
[Ll]ogs/
[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
[Mm]emoryCaptures/
[Rr]ecordings/
ExportedObj/
crashlytics-build.properties

# Burst / IL2CPP / Addressables intermediates
[Bb]urst[Dd]ebug*/
[Ii]l2[Cc]pp*/
unity/Assets/AssetStoreTools*
unity/Assets/StreamingAssets/aa/
unity/Assets/StreamingAssets/aa.meta

# Android build artefacts — hand builds over as a GitHub Release, never a commit.
# A Quest APK is 150–500 MB and changes every build.
*.apk
*.aab

# --- DO COMMIT these, they are small and load-bearing. Never add them above ---
#   unity/Assets/XR/                    XR loader config
#   unity/Packages/manifest.json
#   unity/Packages/packages-lock.json   pins the XR package graph for all six of us
#   unity/ProjectSettings/              including ProjectVersion.txt (everyone on 6000.5.5f1)
#   every .meta file                    GUIDs; lose them and every reference breaks

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IDE / generated solution files
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.csproj
*.unityproj
*.sln
*.suo
*.user
*.userprefs
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.opendb
*.VC.db
*.tmp
.vs/
.idea/
.consulo/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json

# Compiler symbol output. NOTE: .gitattributes routes *.pdb / *.mdb to LFS for
# the rare hand-added native plugin symbol file. .gitignore wins, so those can
# only ever reach LFS via a deliberate `git add -f`. That is intended.
*.pdb
*.mdb

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and signing material — never commit
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.keystore
*.jks

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Merge-tool leftovers (SmartMerge writes these)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.orig
*.rej
*.BACKUP.*
*.BASE.*
*.LOCAL.*
*.REMOTE.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS / editor noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python — ai-service/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 🚨 MODEL WEIGHTS — NEVER COMMIT. Read this before you "just add one file".
#
# WHY: GitHub's Git LFS free tier is 10 GiB of STORAGE and 10 GiB of BANDWIDTH
# per month, billed to the repo OWNER. GitHub Pro does NOT raise it, so the
# Student Developer Pack is not a way out.
#
# Storage counts HISTORY. A weight file committed once is charged forever, even
# after you delete it; undoing it means `git lfs migrate import --everything`
# plus a force-push that rewrites history for all six of us.
#
# The two overages fail completely differently, and STORAGE is the silent one:
#   STORAGE exceeded  -> clones still SUCCEED but hand out ~130-byte pointer
#                        files instead of assets. Unity imports garbage,
#                        materials go magenta, meshes vanish, pushes are
#                        refused. People conclude the repo is broken and
#                        re-clone, which then burns bandwidth too.
#   BANDWIDTH exceeded -> `git lfs pull` errors outright. At least it is loud.
#
# Sizes actually in play here: qwen3:8b is 5.2 GB (it lives in Ollama's own
# store, not in this repo), en_US-lessac-medium.onnx is 63 MB, whisper /
# CTranslate2 weights run 75 MB to 1.5 GB. One 1.5 GB file is 15% of the team's
# entire permanent allowance.
#
# Everyone fetches these locally instead — see docs/SETUP.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.pt
*.pth
ggml-*.bin
model.bin
ai-service/voices/
ai-service/models/
unity/Assets/StreamingAssets/models/

# Piper voices are an .onnx PLUS an .onnx.json sidecar; both are required at
# runtime and neither belongs in git. This also blocks any Unity Sentis .onnx —
# if M5 ever genuinely needs a small on-device net, add a targeted negation
# (!unity/Assets/_Project/Models/foo.onnx) rather than deleting these two lines.
*.onnx
*.onnx.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI service runtime scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ai-service/logs/
ai-service/tmp/
# /converse writes _incoming.wav on every request, and /say output is disposable.
ai-service/**/*.wav
!ai-service/tests/fixtures/*.wav
*.log
.utmp/
.utmp/
Builds/
*_BurstDebugInformation_DoNotShip/
/[Ll]ibrary/
/[Tt]emp/
/[Oo]bj/
/[Bb]uild/
/[Bb]uilds/
/[Ll]ogs/
/[Uu]serSettings/
